    isbefore: []  # f55c
    duplicate_of: []  # f55c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f55c
    pr_ref:  # f55c
    description: "Two CLI-rendering tests are non-hermetic: they pass or fail based on the ambient\ncolor environment (FORCE_COLOR), not on code correctness.\n\nAffected (packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_cli_symbols.py):\n- test_cmd_symbols_truncates_with_message — asserts\n  `'40 additional symbols omitted for brevity' in out`\n- test_cmd_symbols_wrap_flag_renders_full_long_path — asserts the full long path\n  is recoverable from `''.join(out.split())`\n\nRoot cause: cmd_symbols renders via Rich. When color is enabled (this dev\nenvironment exports FORCE_COLOR=3), Rich styles the truncation COUNT separately\nfrom the message text, inserting ANSI reset codes between '40' and ' additional'\n(captured: `\\x1b[1;2;36m40\\x1b[0m\\x1b[2m additional symbols omitted for brevity...`).\nThe test asserts on a contiguous substring, which the interleaved ANSI codes\nbreak. Likewise the wrapped-path test's whitespace-flatten leaves ANSI codes\nembedded, so the long path is not a contiguous substring of the flattened output.\n\nRepro:\n  python3 -m pytest tests/test_cli_symbols.py -q                    -> 2 failed (FORCE_COLOR=3 ambient)\n  env -u FORCE_COLOR -u COLORTERM TERM=dumb python3 -m pytest ...   -> 41 passed\n\nScope/impact: CI is UNAFFECTED — CI stdout is non-tty and does not set\nFORCE_COLOR, so Rich emits no color and both assertions pass; dev is green on CI.\nThis only bites local dev/agents in environments with FORCE_COLOR set, where it\nproduces spurious smart-test failures (exit=1) that can mask real failures and\nwaste investigation time (observed this session while landing WI-lirub).\n\nFix direction (test-hermeticity, NOT a product change — the CLI correctly honors\nFORCE_COLOR): strip ANSI from captured output before the substring assertions, or\nrender the two tests under a forced no-color Rich console. A structural option is\na conftest autouse fixture neutralizing color for CLI-output tests; scope which\nother tests are affected before choosing the layer (only these 2 confirmed in\ntest_cli_symbols.py; a broader CLI-render sweep has not been done).\n\nDiscovered while landing WI-lirub (config_info monorepo heuristic); unrelated to\nthat change."  # f55c
    fields: {}  # f55c
