  message: "Fixed in PR (jgstern-agent/fix/cmd-symbols-test-hermeticity). Root cause: the two tests asserted on Rich-rendered output as contiguous text; under ambient FORCE_COLOR=3 Rich interleaves SGR ANSI reset codes within the text (\\x1b[1;2;36m40\\x1b[0m\\x1b[2m additional symbols...), breaking the substring/whitespace-flatten checks. Fix: local _strip_ansi helper (module _ANSI_SGR regex) applied to captured output before the two assertions. LOCALIZED on purpose — a global no-color conftest fixture was rejected because packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_preview.py legitimately asserts on ANSI output (SVG->PNG->ANSI Chafa pipeline, WI-kulul). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: 'python3 -m pytest tests/test_cli_symbols.py -q' => 41 passed under ambient FORCE_COLOR=3 (was 2 failed) AND 41 passed under 'env -u FORCE_COLOR -u COLORTERM TERM=dumb'. Product behavior unchanged — CLI correctly honors FORCE_COLOR; only the tests were non-hermetic. CI was always green (non-tty)."  # b6fd
